The SM7150's CSIPHY common block carries the sdm845 values

WHAT HAPPENS
------------
The SM7150 fits a CSIPHY version 1.2. Mainline has a lane table of its own for
it (lane_regs_sm7150), but the COMMON BLOCK -the four registers written by hand
in csiphy_lanes_enable()- was left with the sdm845 numbers, which is a CSIPHY
1.0/1.1.

From Qualcomm's driver in the surya's own Android kernel, in
cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy/include/:

    csiphy_common_reg_1_0[]  ->  {0x081C, 0x02}, {0x0800, 0x01, 1ms}, {0x0800, 0x00}
    csiphy_common_reg_1_1[]  ->  the same
    csiphy_common_reg_1_2[]  ->  {0x0814, 0xd5, LANE_ENABLE}
                                 {0x0818, 0x01}
                                 {0x081C, 0x52}          <-- 0x52, not 0x02
                                 {0x0800, 0x03, 1ms}     <-- 0x03 and wait
                                 {0x0800, 0x02, 2PH}     <-- then 0x02
    csiphy_common_reg_1_2_2[]->  same as 1.2

And mainline, in csiphy_lanes_enable():

    ctrl5 (0x814) = 0xd5    matches
    ctrl6 (0x818) = 0x01    matches
    ctrl7 (0x81C) = 0x02    <-- sdm845 value
    ctrl0 (0x800) = 0x00    <-- neither the 0x03 nor the 1 ms wait

The addresses match exactly: CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(0x800, n) is
0x800 + 4n, that is, 0x814, 0x818, 0x81C and 0x800.

WHY IT FITS WHAT WAS MEASURED
-----------------------------
On the surya's front camera (S5K3T2, 4 D-PHY lanes, CSIPHY1):

  - the sensor really does emit: its frame counter advances 30 per second,
  - CSIPHY1 HEARS that sensor: stopping the sensor over I2C with the pipeline
    running drops the interrupts from 8700/s to zero, and they come back when it
    is started again,
  - and the CSID's CSI-2 receiver sees NOTHING: CSI2_RX_IRQ_STATUS = 0x00000000
    with the mask fully open. Not one start-of-transmission sync on any of the
    four lanes, not one packet, not one CRC error.

That ALL FOUR lanes fail at once rules out a single loose data lane and points
at the PHY's common configuration, which is exactly what this patch fixes.

It had been ruled out before, with measurement: the settle count (swept from 16
to 46, flat response), the two positions of the MIPI switch, the supply, and
-checked against that same Qualcomm driver- lane_enable, lane_assign, phy_sel,
the PHY type and every CSID register offset.

The two values also go as module parameters in 0644, because on this device
every reboot is expensive and this way variants can be tried without
recompiling.
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c	2026-08-16 22:38:47.123645135 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c	2026-08-16 22:39:20.969498021 +0200
@@ -1213,6 +1213,20 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Ajustables en caliente para poder probar variantes del bloque comun del
+ * CSIPHY sin recompilar ni reiniciar. -1 = lo que corresponda al SoC.
+ */
+static int ctrl7_valor = -1;
+module_param(ctrl7_valor, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(ctrl7_valor,
+	"Valor de CSI_COMMON_CTRL7 (0x81C). -1 = 0x52 en SM7150, 0x02 en el resto.");
+
+static int secuencia_ctrl0 = -1;
+module_param(secuencia_ctrl0, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(secuencia_ctrl0,
+	"CTRL0 (0x800): 1 = 0x03, esperar 1 ms, 0x02 (como Qualcomm v1.2). 0 = 0x00 (mainline). -1 = segun SoC.");
+
 static void csiphy_lanes_enable(struct csiphy_device *csiphy,
 				struct csiphy_config *cfg,
 				s64 link_freq, u8 lane_mask)
@@ -1237,13 +1251,51 @@
 	writel_relaxed(val, csiphy->base +
 		       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 6));
 
-	val = 0x02;
+	/*
+	 * El SM7150 lleva un CSIPHY v1.2 y estos dos registros del bloque comun
+	 * NO valen lo mismo que en el sdm845 (v1.0/v1.1), que es de donde salen
+	 * los numeros que hay escritos a pelo aqui.
+	 *
+	 * Del driver de Qualcomm del kernel Android del propio surya,
+	 * cam_csiphy_1_2_hwreg.h, csiphy_common_reg_1_2[]:
+	 *
+	 *     {0x0814, 0xd5, ..., CSIPHY_LANE_ENABLE}     <- ctrl5, coincide
+	 *     {0x0818, 0x01, ...}                         <- ctrl6, coincide
+	 *     {0x081C, 0x52, ...}                         <- ctrl7: 0x52, NO 0x02
+	 *     {0x0800, 0x03, delay 1 ms}                  <- ctrl0: 0x03 y esperar
+	 *     {0x0800, 0x02, ..., CSIPHY_2PH_REGS}        <- luego 0x02
+	 *
+	 * Y en las versiones viejas:
+	 *
+	 *     csiphy_common_reg_1_0  ->  {0x081C, 0x02}, {0x0800, 0x01}, {0x0800, 0x00}
+	 *     csiphy_common_reg_1_1  ->  igual
+	 *
+	 * O sea que mainline tiene tabla de carriles propia del SM7150
+	 * (lane_regs_sm7150) pero el bloque comun se quedo con los valores del
+	 * sdm845. Encaja con lo medido: el PHY ve actividad en los carriles
+	 * -para el sensor por I2C y las interrupciones caen a cero- pero no
+	 * consigue un solo sincronismo de inicio, y al CSID no le llega nada.
+	 *
+	 * Los dos valores van como parametros para poder probar variantes en
+	 * caliente: en este movil cada reinicio cuesta caro.
+	 */
+	val = ctrl7_valor >= 0 ? ctrl7_valor :
+	      (csiphy->camss->res->version == CAMSS_7150 ? 0x52 : 0x02);
 	writel_relaxed(val, csiphy->base +
 		       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 7));
 
-	val = 0x00;
-	writel_relaxed(val, csiphy->base +
-		       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
+	if (secuencia_ctrl0 > 0 ||
+	    (secuencia_ctrl0 < 0 && csiphy->camss->res->version == CAMSS_7150)) {
+		writel_relaxed(0x03, csiphy->base +
+			       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
+		usleep_range(1000, 1200);
+		writel_relaxed(0x02, csiphy->base +
+			       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
+	} else {
+		val = 0x00;
+		writel_relaxed(val, csiphy->base +
+			       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
+	}
 
 	if (csiphy_is_gen2(csiphy->camss->res->version))
 		csiphy_gen2_config_lanes(csiphy, settle_cnt);
